# Security Policy

## Supported versions

Security fixes are provided for the latest released version of {{.ProjectName}}.
Older versions may be asked to upgrade before a fix is prepared.

## Reporting a vulnerability

Do not disclose suspected vulnerabilities in a public issue, discussion, pull
request, or merge request.

{{if eq .GitProvider "github"}}
Use the repository's [private vulnerability reporting]({{.ProjectURL}}/security/advisories/new)
channel. If that channel is unavailable, contact a CODEOWNER privately through GitHub.
{{else}}
Use the repository's [private vulnerability reporting]({{.ProjectURL}}/-/security/vulnerability_report)
channel. If that channel is unavailable, contact a CODEOWNER privately through GitLab.
{{end}}

Include the affected version, reproduction steps, impact, and any known mitigation.
Maintainers will acknowledge a complete report as soon as practical and coordinate
disclosure after a fix or mitigation is available.
